  "$comment": [
    "What the asset library contains and how each source becomes a shipped file. Hand-authored; scripts/assets/sources.lock.json is the machine-pinned counterpart (URLs, sha256, licence evidence).",
    "models: tier 'hero' allows 15000 triangles, 'prop' allows 3000. textureSize is the longest side in pixels (1024 for heroes, 512 for small props, 2048 only for a lazily loaded hero). singleSided drops double-sided rendering where the mesh is a closed solid.",
    "surfaces: maps lists what is read from the source; the shipped set is albedo.webp, normal.webp and orm.webp (R occlusion, G roughness, B metalness). size is the albedo edge, normalSize and ormSize default to it. tileMetres is the real-world size of one texture repeat.",
    "Tags: office, corridor, sport, period-1910, period-1971 say where and when an asset belongs. initial-corridor marks the surfaces in the corridor's first download (at most 0.95 MB together); lazy-office marks the Office's lazily loaded set (at most 3 MB together).",
    "Licences: CC0 first. A CC BY entry needs its attribution recorded in the lock entry and must be added to scripts/assets/lib/providers.mjs on purpose."
  ],
